citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Woodworth, R. S. (1938). Experimental Psychology. New York: Holt, Rinehart and Winston. </citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="Fn1"><label>1</label><p>As pointed out by an anonymous reviewer, this may in part be due to some features of the procedure adopted here. The long delay between cues and actions, and the fact that timing cues specified relatively broad intervals instead of specific moments in time may explain the lack of S&#x02013;R binding in our study.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>